# Lab 2: Validation and Error Contracts
# Run these before and after the lab. Before: 201s for bad input, bare 500s, empty 404s.
# After: every failure is application/problem+json with a type, a status, and a traceId.
@host = https://localhost:7001
@ticketId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111

### 400: no title, no requester (before: 201 Created)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "", "description": "Missing fields.", "priority": "Normal", "requesterId": "" }

### 400: a priority that doesn't exist
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Bad priority", "description": "Hmm.", "priority": "Critical", "requesterId": "bob" }

### 400: an urgent ticket needs a real description (FluentValidation, a rule attributes can't express)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Server down", "description": "Help!", "priority": "Urgent", "requesterId": "bob" }

### 400: empty comment
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/comments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "authorId": "dana", "body": "" }

### 404: a ticket that doesn't exist (before: empty body)
GET {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 404: a route that doesn't exist (before: empty body)
GET {{host}}/api/v2/tickets

### Close the seeded ticket (first time: 200)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/close

### 409: close it again (before: 500 with an exception)
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/close

### 409: assign a closed ticket
POST {{host}}/api/v1/tickets/{{ticketId}}/assign
Content-Type: application/json

{ "assigneeId": "dana" }

### 500: an unhandled exception (before: the developer exception page)
GET {{host}}/dev/boom
